} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cbbf209-6f8c-5d7f-bba0-8fe64bcddbb2" :answer-field/key "![Diagram III](images/56/56a3b155e245244e60dcb167ea9efb8944ad2b2bac641ec85555df5b2c260e28.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a60d4465-319d-5ba9-93b8-d257af2c79a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110449" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}$ or ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III represents a line passing through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of  ${R}^{3}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is diagram III only"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db615633-014c-54c3-8cc9-58f82a795b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461635} {:answer/id #uuid "190c9393-acc4-52cd-bef6-50146a4232b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461636}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461636} :answer-field/id #uuid "0185f088-9b2a-5094-b94a-0bc02a21b997" :answer-field/key "![Diagram I](images/40/4099a8ab012d80ceffccda5ac20f6c7f0b9bf7ae5bc0c56dc43e9d023bcdb255.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462571} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "604ec4ba-b242-5e16-9356-f7121d205eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461637} {:answer/id #uuid "46044fb8-965f-5bae-9ba4-b2c07b1b787b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461638}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461637} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7f6e5c5-01f7-5b2a-8d3f-8f42e2d18a10" :answer-field/key "![Diagram II](images/65/65967e3204c569afa63d7aebf80a210d57847c378225969cb63e6bb7ffd1997f.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462572} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a903670-85c8-5ee3-b41e-a7b018550684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461639} {:answer/id #uuid "67525c23-8035-5991-ad29-9bb96ee737f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461640}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461639} :answer-field/id #uuid "85c82fe2-f27f-597c-9d12-860ce869e005" :answer-field/key "![Diagram III](images/18/1800f870abb146524b25756c6949942ca6ab25ff1f5ade92a30e40075d0a0d27.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d94dadb2-4fe3-5787-929d-74b940cbadc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-110597" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}$ or ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I is a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside the given subset. But, \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,\\,-3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is diagram I only"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ad39641-56c0-508c-9b90-0cc2e2767b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461641} {:answer/id #uuid "02252817-c38b-5820-b87f-ed1696a4c751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461642}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461641} :answer-field/id #uuid "857885bf-7367-5e75-8ec5-43d94868cb82" :answer-field/key "![Diagram I](images/43/435ae803182d813230907411b7104b5239d287d294ec69f5d1a0a4112258518a.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73f09b04-09ec-5e1f-bdf5-e3178c28f434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461643} {:answer/id #uuid "01faef8b-4f0b-51b2-80ff-1f9d1ade44d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461644}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461643} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5d5341b-98e6-512b-8142-c17dfa8068d4" :answer-field/key "![Diagram II](images/54/541aa5367d8bb8bd36ea5811579728513153549aa66066d491357f43c5aad11d.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c52a9d4d-a545-519c-8a5a-0c045175f03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461645} {:answer/id #uuid "15b5b644-7d14-50d4-8d39-f862963ee03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461646}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461645} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac97ed8-0d07-5bff-b5b5-97985053e7bd" :answer-field/key "![Diagram III](images/84/8480765d37746d4157a336140609e46919f93ceba05aaed2c595cca8c1e1ccb0.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "153dd84c-6d2a-536b-9c6e-28308cea6f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667858} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e322ae-5573-5b99-9991-25ffc95df55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667859}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186667859} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb18c004-09bf-5415-983e-819c0b6ff7d0" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f37be5a-fb02-59a0-9bc3-1e609a53d6d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110600" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents a set that does not contain the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea812525-5990-52cf-b86e-78f1b4de8995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461647} {:answer/id #uuid "8f213eb6-2142-5889-90e4-c372925d0dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461648}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461647} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9799888-3637-5f54-acd6-ed3396e155dd" :answer-field/key "$A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:xyz=1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af6b52c-a109-53f6-aa27-67a8c43708cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461649} {:answer/id #uuid "ff863854-8a24-5221-be5f-d347d25b3c1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461650}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461650} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c50586-e18a-5fca-a9fa-4b003d93b2c7" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}B=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\\\x+y-z=0\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462578} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f70460d9-df3a-58dd-95a2-bafff6dc83d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461651} {:answer/id #uuid "61868caa-f76b-5288-8ca4-5d353e006f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461652}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461651} :answer-field/id #uuid "18092fb5-74d5-5ff7-870d-5e5eab99935e" :answer-field/key "$C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:y=-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3d55fbe8-7170-5840-8a9a-b1f2a55c58fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-110611" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $xyz=1$ since $0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x+y-z=0$ since $0+0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $y=-1$ since $0\\ne -1.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{gathered}B=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\\\x+y-z=0\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247159 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ba35c72-4811-55d0-b2b1-fb8116a2cc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461653} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2a422a-84a1-5671-bc55-3b45224e58cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461654}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461653} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0888cfa-5fff-5bcc-9c6f-d3cf0a398b99" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}A=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\\\x-4y=1\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462580} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2974aa62-0b1f-5343-a4a5-c39a1584c078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461655} {:answer/id #uuid "78c8ebf0-1d54-5046-ae1c-3426546d3565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461656}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461656} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad91d256-6b2d-51b9-8149-c46bca013503" :answer-field/key "$B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x=-2y\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5784de9d-74b4-5c34-9c61-2b2f1a7172ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461657} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa10535-80e6-5c1d-a5e9-5bed7b7ca613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461658}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461657} :answer-field/id #uuid "822bc400-c192-58d1-80df-f14e9a428a6a" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}C=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\\\{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "49bd226a-4547-5889-a62c-e6c2912a1520" :question/math-academy-id "q-110760" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each subset.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. For instance, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $x-4y=1$ since $0-4\\cdot 0=0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x=-2y$ since $0=-2\\cdot 0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace. No point in ${R}^{3}$ satisfies the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0.$ Hence, $C=∅.$ The empty set is not a subspace since it does not contain the zero vector.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x=-2y\\}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6d33351-e47b-5dcf-8a4d-d3e61f058c5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461659} {:answer/id #uuid "d95202b2-7ac0-51a9-beba-433590fd067c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461660}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461659} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc7a303b-9974-55fa-9193-b45a893b05b7" :answer-field/key "$A={⟨2t,2+t⟩\\,:\\,t\\in R}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27c0fe0f-a14e-5a97-bb81-d2b618017a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461661} {:answer/id #uuid "52cb8444-2346-56eb-8483-17ca5a3815c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461662}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461662} :answer-field/id #uuid "df43bab4-a790-5959-8eef-b12b9e48205b" :answer-field/key "$B={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x-y=0}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c438405c-079c-5cda-acfc-5fc8f4718e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461663} {:answer/id #uuid "688e99c6-1ace-56a4-a978-0e19e70df677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461664}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461663} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fcae7ac-a05d-5215-8944-c0e4000c37c6" :answer-field/key "$C={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:y=1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc11ea3b-3ee9-5cb9-a26d-3aab9cb82498" :question/math-academy-id "q-110761" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. If the origin belongs to this subset, we would have, for some $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2t \\\\ 2+t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2t &=0 \\\\ 2+t &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe see that the system has no solution. So, $0$ is not in $A.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace.  It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x-y=0$ since $0-0=0.$ So, $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $y=1$ since $0\\ne 1.$ So, $0$ is not in $C.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $B={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x-y=0}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d9730b-5dfb-533b-84b4-820508c681c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-j-2k)=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259940} {:answer/id #uuid "0b43e2e4-7d7c-5a06-9a4e-e5d5bd6fd688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k)=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259978} {:answer/id #uuid "1cb6f84d-39e2-5454-9223-e2660394500e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k)=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260120} {:answer/id #uuid "7625d753-d05c-5241-a7d8-009db644319a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (5i-3j+2k)=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260906} {:answer/id #uuid "d5cf573a-806c-58e0-a8bf-e4a86fe1818d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i+2j-3k)=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259978} :answer-field/id #uuid "149da6bf-b3f7-50a5-a4bd-3e9aa558c141" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5600d5c-cd95-56af-a0e8-ae34bd21b34c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127632" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(\\sqrt{5},-1,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=\\sqrt{5}i-j+2k,$ and $n=\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k) & =(\\sqrt{5}i-j+2k)\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k) \\\\ r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k) & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fe78bf8-7ac3-5189-bff3-2c01abd83f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260556} {:answer/id #uuid "55d1fef6-f7ac-57bb-b250-1ef2f14cdf76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-5,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260608} {:answer/id #uuid "569921ed-c576-5fb7-89fc-7dc8845f8c9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,5,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260615} {:answer/id #uuid "6e32f91d-e1b8-5637-bf32-c747b24cff0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,0,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260844} {:answer/id #uuid "d4da54f4-6265-5fdb-8cdc-b74a0d4db467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,5,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261751}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260608} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a037ed-685c-5ce7-8e35-ec4164485d85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "afcc8d33-fe9b-5c65-a7f2-97b6d0a1032f" :question/math-academy-id "q-127861" :question/problem "Find $(3b-c)\\times (9a-2b)$, if $a\\times b=⟨0,0,1⟩$, $a\\times c=⟨0,-1,3⟩$ and $c\\times b=⟨0,2,0⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\na\\times a=0.\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3b-c)\\times (9a-2b) &= ((3b)\\times (9a))-((3b)\\times (2b))-(c\\times (9a))+(c\\times (2b))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3b-c)\\times (9a-2b) &= ((3b)\\times (9a))-((3b)\\times (2b))-(c\\times (9a))+(c\\times (2b)) \\\\ &= (3\\cdot 9)(b\\times a)-(3\\cdot 2)(b\\times b)-9(c\\times a)+2(c\\times b) \\\\ &= 27(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b)-9(c\\times a)+2(c\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $b\\times b=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b)-9(c\\times a)+2(c\\times b) &= -27(a\\times b)-6(0)+9(a\\times c)+2(c\\times b) \\\\ &= -27(a\\times b)+9(a\\times c)+2(c\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-27(a\\times b)+9(a\\times c)+2(c\\times b) &= -27⟨0,0,1⟩+9⟨0,-1,3⟩+2⟨0,2,0⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨0,0,-27⟩+⟨0,-9,27⟩+⟨0,4,0⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨0,-5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1db4c2af-2e78-5ec5-8ede-f1aff92a3bae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260130} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4df1a9-277d-5ebc-8864-b31c9ef3bafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260540} {:answer/id #uuid "86ae6e82-65b8-5c01-9bd6-0496eaf7bc36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261049} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ab9526-555f-538e-8473-1cc8d4c5b366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261494} {:answer/id #uuid "f9ced82e-1eb9-51cb-8708-d7eb16c14606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262056}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260130} :answer-field/id #uuid "40642ce9-2755-5ebb-8afd-84006382c910" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e0d1c80-eb5c-5bda-b21b-a06adaec16d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127873" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,-2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28523b60-9c94-5e08-8811-eeb6c2c8385b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260229} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6f925d-2385-5203-beed-2ae656f27e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260554} {:answer/id #uuid "71ffe7bc-2035-50b5-afb6-f098f001c957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260872} {:answer/id #uuid "c1024317-bb4d-5e9d-b670-c092e80227c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261578} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc3f903-0607-5523-bb23-e9a27fc580dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260229} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e71e846-7ac8-5f2e-bf8c-340173700a84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1298261d-fd1d-57fd-8c0d-689d1739fab9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127888" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩=\\sqrt{2}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩=\\sqrt{2}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨3,2,-1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1066db60-12af-5e82-a7c0-d24afa450e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260024} {:answer/id #uuid "336d23d9-d848-54ca-86e6-782c1b13a369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260339} {:answer/id #uuid "6bfd83ea-5bb5-57e7-b814-e0e365ce1b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260820} {:answer/id #uuid "d4093fa7-7b24-5445-bf63-718de7a82e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261744} {:answer/id #uuid "f03309e1-ca15-5335-aab5-a2535a4337a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261981}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260339} :answer-field/id #uuid "f46674a6-7e2b-5656-b018-7f5bf5e7afa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa3bed00-1af4-5c46-8c12-264209634c51" :question/math-academy-id "q-127910" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,1,3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1} & ={t}_{2}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{2},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨3,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2beba37f-86cf-5232-87f0-3a72cad6aa1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260265} {:answer/id #uuid "3388728b-fa84-5463-ad08-b7f075149767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260342} {:answer/id #uuid "69593a3f-9b3e-5e03-9feb-98b4870ba2e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260795} {:answer/id #uuid "7850ba65-684f-536f-99f4-bd2f68dda967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260926} {:answer/id #uuid "c555ef85-87ee-5b9d-892c-6ac228026dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261616}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260265} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a41bb79-1d8e-5e75-a39b-9f8ce0aeeb7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1c9c582-8595-5cfb-925f-05282f9b76e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-127911" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,2⟩=\\sqrt{11}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,2⟩=\\sqrt{11}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,2,2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}+2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =2{t}_{2}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨2{t}_{2}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{2},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{2},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨2,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262853 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aa825cb-f5f2-5941-b18f-a35a9e8ffaab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,-4,3⟩=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260107} {:answer/id #uuid "394ffd1f-3104-5495-902a-37954445a0c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,4⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260385} {:answer/id #uuid "56cda873-6a65-51e4-b130-2eb9c208d8a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,4,4⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260617} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2cec22-6b83-56cf-81ae-8596b434a0ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,4⟩=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261696} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b3d4ad-159b-554b-a0a1-ef2fb9a85ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261900}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261900} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f4a93d8-207b-5307-acbb-b861f6a8320e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9164c795-7f61-5d54-9538-2653e37cb486" :question/math-academy-id "q-127927" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1)$, we can find a vector that is parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,-3,1⟩-⟨4,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨3,-4,4⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =⟨1,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262855 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0387b95b-ea4c-5624-9fdd-7d44aae31856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,1,1⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259907} {:answer/id #uuid "ad85ebfc-775c-5bdb-a5e6-836a5963e43c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,5⟩=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261395} {:answer/id #uuid "b2a79415-12c6-5171-8ecf-e701971bbaad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,3,1⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261452} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ba12b0-dcfe-5c43-b282-17a43fb1d275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261796} {:answer/id #uuid "eb666347-2e39-5891-a53f-4830ffc6eb6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,5,1⟩=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261942}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261796} :answer-field/id #uuid "207a2b37-6c4f-5b41-aa59-d8127027f268" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "57b46f7d-b75a-5f5c-87e6-c8948d671ea4" :question/math-academy-id "q-127936" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-2,5)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-3,0,2)$ and $B(2,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-2,5⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-3,0,2)$ and $B(2,1,3)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,1,3⟩-⟨-3,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨5,1,1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ & =⟨3,-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a6d49af-f4b3-58b7-98b0-926d7d2ec1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,3⟩=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259966} {:answer/id #uuid "bfef5be5-9f0c-5938-9df5-2b2093f08bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261571} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b1b7f5-3316-5749-a268-d9545bd6066b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,1⟩=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261585} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe23397-9a20-5f8a-922d-81c869029405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,1,4⟩=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261671} {:answer/id #uuid "da6e68b1-4c37-525a-a289-ddc6a1494083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,4,3⟩=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261805}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261571} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f2421e2-84aa-5ab7-a62e-bbab5487c4bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf1b6add-bb69-5029-a7d5-1bf17a1142b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127944" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-1,1,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-3t \\\\ y &=2+4t \\\\ z &=-3+t.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-1,1,2⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-3t \\\\ y &=2+4t \\\\ z &=-3+t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨5,2,-3⟩+t\\text{ }\\underbrace{⟨-3,4,1⟩}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-3,4,1⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-3,4,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ & =⟨-1,1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51d54e99-47fd-5196-bed2-224f8e8d6e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-5,6⟩=-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260567} {:answer/id #uuid "6596da01-bdc7-5092-85c8-ed385e549481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-5,6,4⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260757} {:answer/id #uuid "a4dec472-388c-5244-92b0-6f09b899dc4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261308} {:answer/id #uuid "c353e3c0-705b-5a2d-8f53-481fb42f2778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-6,4,5⟩=28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261602} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5dca95-d508-5c38-8c43-2d7a75def3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,5,-4⟩=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262106}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261308} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd45dac4-6ba8-5e19-9d05-285dc1c5817a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4425e14a-832e-5d34-b997-7b779cec15dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-127948" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-3,2,1)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1+6t \\\\ y &=3-5t \\\\ z &=-2+4t.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-3,2,1⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1+6t \\\\ y &=3-5t \\\\ z &=-2+4t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,-2⟩+t\\text{ }\\underbrace{⟨6,-5,4⟩}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65e4dacb-b64f-5663-ae54-844ec9e37c4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,4⟩=22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260760} {:answer/id #uuid "a344d6d0-c843-57a0-87ed-6643487a6ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,1⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261298} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b752a4-52ea-54e2-96dc-81dc14098d76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,1⟩=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261313} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9815dd-2b59-5495-91a4-c387e6882786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,-2⟩=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261371} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f71bee-c234-59c3-9e78-d739bf030e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261577}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261577} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e498358-75ca-5ef1-ae02-06dee6634086" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7885abf5-baa7-59dd-be20-bec3451c5be4" :question/math-academy-id "q-127956" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(4,-2,3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1+2t \\\\ y &=3-2t \\\\ z &=5+t.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨4,-2,3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1+2t \\\\ y &=3-2t \\\\ z &=5+t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,5⟩+t\\text{ }\\underbrace{⟨2,-2,1⟩}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨2,-2,1⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨2,-2,1⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d071325-4ae4-5964-a64f-fab8d162533c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-3y+2z-7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260960} {:answer/id #uuid "be614cfc-c9fb-5c76-8dee-684a30dc17e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-3y+z-17=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261553} {:answer/id #uuid "ce192468-5857-54ba-b341-740fd51b914a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-y+2z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261695} {:answer/id #uuid "e488cd1b-dabd-58e2-8323-9fd47b3dbc39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y+3z-15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261885} {:answer/id #uuid "ed08e876-cf68-52de-82e6-d95fc85813d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y+z-13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261957}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261695} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ed27435-6a6b-5a91-82c1-435b9c8e60ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1247c7f3-ac99-5899-948f-91e6b23f17f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-127964" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(5,2,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=3i-j+2k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨5,2,-1⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨3,-1,2⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =⟨5,2,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =11 \\\\ 3x-y+2z & =11 \\\\ 3x-y+2z-11 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "411ca382-bf09-5d64-b04e-118a15b82b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+3y-z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260445} {:answer/id #uuid "54d729d8-bf79-548c-abf5-c9240fb50b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-3y-z+13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260594} {:answer/id #uuid "6751b20c-2d88-5607-b734-7aa1b9059535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-4y-z+9=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260778} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc5e1ea-63d3-5013-af1d-ebfbe1c3d3ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+4y-z-7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261690} {:answer/id #uuid "ce059a59-2378-51c5-9efb-e24a7f0e20ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+3y-4z-17=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261694}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261690} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f194fa4-7f96-5976-a4a3-abc6280aecc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d060436d-551e-5fcb-9a99-c81961b307b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127967" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-2,3,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=3i+4j-k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-2,3,-1⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨3,4,-1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ & =⟨-2,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ & =7 \\\\ 3x+4y-z & =7 \\\\ 3x+4y-z-7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d51072c-883a-525a-8646-40e5c82ad4e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+7y-2z+15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260127} {:answer/id #uuid "6326b3cd-0214-5827-9d35-baed2ba8695e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+7y+z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260728} {:answer/id #uuid "8d5aca35-27e9-5c23-aff5-e71d615f9cfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7x-2y-z+19=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261109} {:answer/id #uuid "91ea860c-4845-50a4-a075-2bb871d412bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+7y-z-14=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261144} {:answer/id #uuid "d95aedb2-04eb-5ef6-a10d-ec449203a494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+2y-7z-7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261794}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261144} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8e68f4b-4cc2-5e45-b811-88d387aeee6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7e0ef36-c57e-59d2-a0fa-0b27cc7256a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-127971" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-2,1,-3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨-2,7,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-2,1,-3⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨-2,7,-1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ & =⟨-2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,7,-1⟩ & =14 \\\\ -2x+7y-z & =14 \\\\ -2x+7y-z-14 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03fc24ad-0a55-5ba6-86e2-72a7e2faa119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y+7z+10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259912} {:answer/id #uuid "66d86e94-8732-54fa-bd6e-cefef51a308b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+7z+5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260772} {:answer/id #uuid "6c7b8d10-0fc7-5e18-a928-bc79f2161f52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+7y-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260827} {:answer/id #uuid "872e0d66-ed64-5fa5-9fa4-d541c030c090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+7z+20=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261053} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d3d9de-db57-5987-ac48-3ee9c443029a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7x+7y+7z-20=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261502}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261053} :answer-field/id #uuid "64f04d84-a350-591e-8cad-0290a83a08b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c46eaba-babf-598a-bbbb-00b2297bd0d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-128375" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,0,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=7-2t \\\\ y &=7 \\\\ z &=7t\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,0,-2⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨-2,0,7⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨-2,0,7⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ & =⟨3,0,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,0,7⟩ & =-20 \\\\ -2x+7z & =-20 \\\\ -2x+7z+20 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c68694d-6618-534f-92a7-bd2167bf9cfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x-y+z+1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260664} {:answer/id #uuid "9668328b-dd01-52ef-a2f2-c043826d2c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y-z+3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261178} {:answer/id #uuid "98a8daa1-6508-5a17-a74c-7d0641516440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y-z+6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261198} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d37a90-e0f8-5347-9040-4a09d7753dc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y+z-6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261296} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e2401c-4add-51dd-8da3-6fcbf664c2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261362}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261198} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a505006-158e-56ec-be3a-13c758fba6b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c43ec9b4-fb75-54f1-9dd3-fda6dabf447d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128376" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-5,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3+t \\\\ y &=t \\\\ z &=7-t\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,-5,2⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨1,1,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨1,1,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-5,2⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ & =-6 \\\\ x+y-z & =-6 \\\\ x+y-z+6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f87268c-9742-5090-b7cb-521a5d8bbe66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,4,-4⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260021} {:answer/id #uuid "a390ff13-0937-5eb3-b38b-3df5883b8889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨-4,4,-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261300} {:answer/id #uuid "def43d7d-583f-5acb-a4e0-a37562571a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,-2,4⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261844} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c13bd5-c05b-5f70-93b5-0ba177da222f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262013} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcc7a65-376c-57d0-ac3e-a501019e18ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,2⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262119}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262013} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b80e560-2ad7-58b7-9b2c-28eb67acbc7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f6aca53-4308-58bc-afcc-f2738d69d1e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-128380" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $4x+4y-2z=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨4,4,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+4y-2z & =0 \\\\ 2z & =4x+4y \\\\ z & =2x+2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=0.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262890 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "651b8de1-bfcf-5968-bd65-75bfaff53a19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-21⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,0,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260747} {:answer/id #uuid "85a251a4-8626-5a48-8978-5be3141abf43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-15⟩)\\cdot ⟨-1,5,0⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261035} {:answer/id #uuid "96ee2d72-498d-5cd2-92b2-c9ee6d6979c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,-1,5⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261182} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d35c29-d1ec-5549-bbc6-6fa5edd439de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,11⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261274} {:answer/id #uuid "f35bd877-7bda-5cdd-bb0d-81ebd993a270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,17⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262002}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262002} :answer-field/id #uuid "922d17c5-e5bc-5723-a873-fd95d3df5865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fda593ff-14ab-57bf-9851-b4c04717562e" :question/math-academy-id "q-128383" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $5y-z+17=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨0,5,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-z+17 & =0 \\\\ z & =5y+17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $y=0$, we get $z=17.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,17)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,17⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,17⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,-1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141dbd48-41d3-5f2d-ac44-58651f4076fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-2y+6z+21=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260051} {:answer/id #uuid "2c33e216-d94a-5531-8c09-2b026bb2f73c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-6y-2z+17=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260271} {:answer/id #uuid "d74c1003-0d34-55fd-8cf1-e3b806cfd4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-2y-6z+10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261767} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf6af12-e362-5602-b7d5-5d61a520a968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-6y-2z+7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261821} {:answer/id #uuid "f70483bf-7393-5c2b-b762-0a3626381ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-4y-6z+13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262035}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261767} :answer-field/id #uuid "b802df34-fc9c-5dbb-a3bf-830e576b7529" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25936c54-3b79-59fa-98c2-e2c44069022a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128462" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(1,-2,3)$, $P(3,-1,4)$ and $Q(-1,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨1,-2,3⟩,\\,p=⟨3,-1,4⟩,$ and $q=⟨-1,0,1⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,4⟩-⟨1,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩-⟨1,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-4i+2j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-4,2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,2,6⟩ & =⟨3,-1,4⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,2,6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,2,6⟩ & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,2,6⟩ & =10 \\\\ -4x+2y+6z & =10 \\\\ -4x+2y+6z-10 & =0 \\\\ 4x-2y-6z+10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3378948b-825a-55cf-9663-c807418b87a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,5,3⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨3,1,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260340} {:answer/id #uuid "551ccc15-6c0c-5039-88a2-7c2277d3cc86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,3,5⟩+s⟨1,-4,2⟩+t⟨1,3,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260600} {:answer/id #uuid "652fe9f5-e2ab-5dde-b696-8ea97d54ea0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-5,3⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨3,-1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260750} {:answer/id #uuid "f69083bb-4761-5bf3-9039-f5f20cabe505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-3,5⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨1,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262032} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9f7527-9312-5746-98df-ee945a4f2092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-5,3⟩+s⟨4,2,1⟩+t⟨1,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262098}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262032} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfb59e1a-3963-5aad-97e9-5f5d072dde2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77bbe80b-345c-53b5-9d37-d2d8ccf32ea9" :question/math-academy-id "q-128463" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-3,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨2,4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,3,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $p=⟨2,-3,5⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,3,-1⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,-3,5⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨1,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262903 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bff57da-7142-583e-97e0-f0fed4e62ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-3,4⟩+s⟨1,1,-1⟩+t⟨1,4.5,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259988} {:answer/id #uuid "440085c5-69ce-533e-a9e2-401daef39de5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-3,4⟩+s⟨1,5,-1⟩+t⟨1,2.5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260465} {:answer/id #uuid "8dff161b-2f18-5c00-9912-1cddaca567e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,-2,4⟩+s⟨1,-5,-1⟩+t⟨1,1,2.5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261118} {:answer/id #uuid "e8308ab4-dd45-5d95-8f7c-7246803b9a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-4,3⟩+s⟨2,5,-1⟩+t⟨2,2.5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261910} {:answer/id #uuid "ed64b2a5-cc56-526d-9cd6-527689bacfbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,4,-3⟩+s⟨5,-1,1⟩+t⟨2.5,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261959}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260465} :answer-field/id #uuid "7751d20d-1bb8-5c8a-a0e4-e7a495a1a00e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5cb8725-9c1f-539e-b05a-c7e9f146df91" :question/math-academy-id "q-128464" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-3,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨1,5,-1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,2.5,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $p=⟨2,-3,4⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨1,5,-1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,2.5,1⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,-3,4⟩+s⟨1,5,-1⟩+t⟨1,2.5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25e556cd-a391-5917-822b-8f0c58a17864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260206} {:answer/id #uuid "3874529d-2cd1-5e52-b994-a124c92f6d1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260376} {:answer/id #uuid "809538a6-d29e-5ae1-a625-76cad949f419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260995} {:answer/id #uuid "b61663fc-53a4-59f7-9749-9a9396b71f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261475} {:answer/id #uuid "e68a2f9d-b3e8-5770-b7f8-b4076894dde0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261898}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260995} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cc6175f-10c8-52b0-97bc-eb699a3d3f65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6be53925-8dd1-5560-9da9-12cc0fe0c84f" :question/math-academy-id "q-128467" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $S(1,-3,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$  and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $S$ is $p=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$  and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "663205e4-4973-5040-b28f-cda4c8a8fbe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,-3,-23⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260764} {:answer/id #uuid "701e1886-1ef3-59a2-b9e0-5082885a8a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,3,-21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260859} {:answer/id #uuid "e465b55e-9846-5383-9fec-f3e3618baf10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-19,-1,17⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261883} {:answer/id #uuid "fd74070d-627c-5d09-b3c6-7a6b40a5eb01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,1,-13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262095} {:answer/id #uuid "fe26eb23-b15c-592a-ac69-99a33f59a87b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,-1,-23⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262103}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262103} :answer-field/id #uuid "58b5e38b-a867-52fe-baad-a9657fbdda5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a100465f-b165-5424-a64a-cc08ceec83b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-128495" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨1,7,-2⟩+t⟨-3,4,1⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-3,4,1⟩$ and $w=⟨5,1,-2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-9i-j-23k \\\\  & =⟨-9,-1,-23⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-9,-1,-23⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b4a3c41-2d3e-5406-a2cd-cbab49cb529e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,-4,-26⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260257} {:answer/id #uuid "63d710f5-99cb-53b4-8290-6299023ee722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,-2,17⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260737} {:answer/id #uuid "95c11743-7580-55cc-a7f1-587f795b6ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-2,-22⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261175} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1ed729-7d24-5fef-a919-3b87d20a7b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,2,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261244} {:answer/id #uuid "da606c57-af3e-52fa-9552-99fdba561ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-8,-7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261803}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261175} :answer-field/id #uuid "e859b94c-82b3-57fc-b159-f1a0791b5216" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58d7da64-39e5-5263-82e1-d46d43bc9c9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128497" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,\\sqrt{7},-2⟩+t⟨-2,8,0⟩+s⟨3,-1,-1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,8,0⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-1,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-8i-2j-22k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "259294bf-42a6-5b1f-a914-2eeba4786e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,12,-7⟩+s⟨1,3,-5⟩+t⟨1,6,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260203} {:answer/id #uuid "3660d937-cc87-5a73-a31f-13375df8d401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260360} {:answer/id #uuid "586437d1-d3c1-5c04-82a5-9e97897d0755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨-3,4,2⟩+t⟨1,5,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260630} {:answer/id #uuid "5a80a400-edf2-5ed4-95ef-bc093dec6a28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨3,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260648} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a3a0fb-37c8-5001-bfec-42aa7883b3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-3,5,1⟩+t⟨1,6,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261347}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260360} :answer-field/id #uuid "991622fb-4bb5-597a-a633-df7720b54e4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75465043-c7d7-54b7-b914-8b78a961bb97" :question/math-academy-id "q-128536" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(-7,12,-3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,2,4⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-22,17,13⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-5,3,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,5,6⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-7,12,-3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-7,12,-3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09eff712-270d-559e-b2ed-1b87d24b561f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-7,6,-3⟩+t⟨-9,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259965} {:answer/id #uuid "7aaf24c1-4af3-5471-a6e4-7bbde47ce0bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,6,-7⟩+t⟨-4,9,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260946} {:answer/id #uuid "ac345a14-1f68-5fe2-8828-2ef99a48c407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,7,-6⟩+t⟨-4,3,9⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261380} {:answer/id #uuid "bc74f471-d5ff-5ade-bba5-ec27b6ff5caf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨6,3,-7⟩+t⟨-3,9,4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261534} {:answer/id #uuid "da3efea4-2fb6-5260-9315-bcfe7be8b9f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨3,7,-6⟩+t⟨-4,3,9⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261802}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260946} :answer-field/id #uuid "859eebf0-098a-5a3c-8e3c-589906da5209" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "016cb0cc-72ee-551e-911e-dc0a1ad297a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-128743" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(7,-2,3),\\,V(4,4,-4),$ and $W(3,7,6).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{UW},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨4,4,-4⟩-⟨7,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,6,-7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{UW} & =⟨3,7,6⟩-⟨7,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,9,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨7,-2,3⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+s\\overset{\\to }{UV}+t\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,6,-7⟩+t⟨-4,9,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03170ce6-1b74-5d0c-a740-266903fa4105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,4,2⟩+t⟨4,-4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259902} {:answer/id #uuid "31b47527-c857-57e6-abe0-41faa15df975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨4,2,6⟩+t⟨-4,-3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260322} {:answer/id #uuid "3648beed-e103-5bec-8bc9-7ee681a02fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260359} {:answer/id #uuid "7a29aab3-eefc-5ee1-beae-88249bb83af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260941} {:answer/id #uuid "a7218829-3284-55b3-b600-8e4433336662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,2,4⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261332}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260359} :answer-field/id #uuid "0824088c-267c-5eb4-919f-03962a76134c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e20b81af-d8f6-5935-a0ab-531fc6f636f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-128760" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(5,3,1)$ and $V(2,-1,-3),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨2,-1,-3⟩-⟨5,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨5,3,1⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262929 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a9595c5-d8f6-5617-b156-92b53851b716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260250} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce9642e-12a2-5cdf-b2c6-8d924f99cc04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨2,\\sqrt{5},-3⟩+t⟨4,-2,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260672} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbdf40e-542c-5dc2-a6fd-921cd50285d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-4,2,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in 