#edb/ref 17592186285699} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c1dc785-3432-52e4-acff-92a4cfbb35ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c15957e5-b917-5445-9850-6ff678f7a755" :question/math-academy-id "q-181687" :question/problem "![](images/f6/f6a3b3bc0064525271804e6d20689c21ca84c0adad138a8bd8d398be66e45c3e.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-x-1\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,x+2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x-1$ and *below* the line $y=x+2.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x-1,\\,y<x+2.\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-x-1<y<x+2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is not included in the set (the lines are dashed), the inequalities are strict.\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x-1<y<x+2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e53d49-a131-5b22-8032-7c46e048c20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284843} {:answer/id #uuid "2a3a41c1-c4b5-5356-bfa1-c588f3dcba2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285158} {:answer/id #uuid "365c747b-3953-581f-aef5-c73b4645b4e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285290} {:answer/id #uui