" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285321} {:answer/id #uuid "553afa5a-4338-5c57-b279-ff0312e09a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285569} {:answer/id #uuid "811b0f7f-9402-5653-bc54-13686f987440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285974} {:answer/id #uuid "e236c333-2153-5146-b193-5ef3d6ec8ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286848} {:answer/id #uuid "efd75d20-6069-5efc-a801-26f5c278e695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286988}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285321} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab7d9b8-1d47-56d4-a66f-0f80a739dcdf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dab3d6dc-4b31-53f2-8ab3-bc64485c9198" :question/math-academy-id "q-181688" :question/problem "![](images/46/4628a6e45445a585361f7d32586b27e29bc726d4ed8b7f072679e5537df59644.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x+1\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,3x\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=x+1$ and *below* the line $y=3x.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>x+1,\\,y<3x.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\nx+1<y<3x.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=3x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\nx+1<y\\le 3x\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+1<y\\le 3x\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b7a7422-0bcf-5706-ae8f-72c9ece61bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285166} {:answer/id #uuid "2d166e9a-fcd9-5b6d-89d1-3e838ceada86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285186} {:answer/id #uuid "626c9538-6fdc-52f9-9f52-20ce738bf7eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285689} {:answer/id #uuid "9a12840e-a2c3-50de-9e43-87a31770bd26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286199} {:answer/id #uuid "cf4b0e6c-806d-5a0b-ae15-ee9ed923b4a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286671}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285689} :answer-field/id #uuid "19da688f-4cba-51c2-8892-be4247f77378" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0014d307-5e77-586a-b23e-f2aba6c41f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284789} {:answer/id #uuid "01b659a3-1590-57ce-b570-119d57e48981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284803} {:answer/id #uuid "039df918-b1da-5c3e-a883-a65e7d757d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498