culty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "281f8e94-72c2-5b73-8bcb-5cb4814a0f37" :question/math-academy-id "q-181689" :question/problem "![](images/32/32168a2cb1fe14dbc88725347611ae5951198e81dfaa0b41e780106750bbb741.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,3x\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,\\frac{x}{4}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=3x$ and *below* the line $y=\\frac{x}{4}.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>3x,\\,y<\\frac{x}{4}.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n3x<y<\\frac{x}{4}.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=3x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n3x\\le y<\\frac{x}{4}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3x\\le y<\\frac{x}{4}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287726 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e0f3e55-2f5d-5cc2-a6c2-4ec49f624ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285196} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e5ef37-95f1-50b2-b2c2-51e62aac2eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286257} {:answer/id #uuid "a9222ec9-3dd0-55a9-9265-77dc50ccbf7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286329} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e31e4b-076f-5d73-9576-e17fe67ed983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286