#edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285531} {:answer/id #uuid "6519603a-a368-5577-a6f9-f60eb8e8349f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285706} {:answer/id #uuid "740031a5-6fce-5b6a-ab1a-c7320b6f3464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285858} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b02fa1-c592-5def-9031-7190016ea776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286771}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285531} :answer-field/id #uuid "e39c74c8-0985-569c-b97d-0b781f39df50" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "80918b0e-9572-56bb-b137-be14e694fe5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-181791" :question/problem "![](images/af/af3a9e323fa460b60bfa900c7edbcceb4057c442803160b2b4b5bd0704b4db7c.png)\n\nDescribe the set of points shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}},\\,{{field-4}}\\le y\\le {{field-5}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points $P(x,y)$ satisfy the condition\n\n$$\nx\\in {-1,0,1,2},\\,y\\in {-2,-1,0,1,2,3}.\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n$$\n-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16485085-1400-54fb-bbf0-300092083449" :answer